-- coa2-ch3-similarity.l4: Part 5, Chapter 3 (Similarity to other names), ss 66-74,
-- lines 743-876 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.  LAYER 1: the law, objectively; no point of view.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".  Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words.
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording).  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Seams taken as inputs: s 1121 "officer in default" (coa24).  Judgments the Act hands to the Secretary of State,
-- to a company names adjudicator or to the court are plain inputs, never guessed.
-- Every name that is not in coa-core.l4 begins with the section label it implements.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Similarity to other name on registrar's index (ss 66-68)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:745 | 66 Name not to be the same as another in the index
-- src:746 | (1) A company must not be registered under this Act by a name that is the same as another name appearing in the registrar's index of company names.
@ref s 66(1) Name not to be the same as another in the index (src:745-746)
GIVEN `the name is the same as another name appearing in the registrar's index of company names (regulations under subsection (2) may say what is disregarded and what counts as the same)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `registration by the name is permitted by regulations under subsection (4) (specified circumstances or specified consent)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(1) the company may be registered by the name` MEANS
    IF `registration by the name is permitted by regulations under subsection (4) (specified circumstances or specified consent)`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- points outside the text: s 66(4)(a) says the regulations may permit registration by a name otherwise prohibited under this section
    ELSE IF `the name is the same as another name appearing in the registrar's index of company names (regulations under subsection (2) may say what is disregarded and what counts as the same)`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must not be registered under this Act by a name that is the same as another name appearing in the registrar's index of company names"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition names only a name that is the same as another name in the index

