@ref s 66(6) "specified" (src:758-758)
GIVEN `specified in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66(6) the circumstances or consent are specified` MEANS
    IF `specified in the regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this section “specified” means specified in the regulations"

-- src:759 | 67 Power to direct change of name in case of similarity to existing name
-- src:760 | (1) The Secretary of State may direct a company to change its name if it has been registered in a name that is the same as or, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, too like—
-- src:761 | (a) a name appearing at the time of the registration in the registrar's index of company names, or
-- src:762 | (b) a name that should have appeared in that index at that time.
@ref s 67(1) Power to direct change of name in case of similarity to existing name (src:759-762)
GIVEN `the company has been registered in a name that is the same as a name in (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the Secretary of State the name is too like a name in (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name in question appeared at the time of the registration in the registrar's index of company names` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the name in question should have appeared in that index at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(1) the Secretary of State may direct the company to change its name` MEANS
    IF       (    `the company has been registered in a name that is the same as a name in (a) or (b)`
              OR  `in the opinion of the Secretary of State the name is too like a name in (a) or (b)`)
         AND (    `the name in question appeared at the time of the registration in the registrar's index of company names`
              OR  `the name in question should have appeared in that index at that time`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary of State may direct a company to change its name if it has been registered in a name that is the same as or, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, too like— (a) ... or (b) ..." (fork 11: the other reading is JUST FALSE, a failed "if" read as the text\'s own no)

