-- src:776 | 68 Direction to change name: supplementary provisions
-- src:777 | (1) The following provisions have effect in relation to a direction under section 67 (power to direct change of name in case of similarity to existing name).
-- src:778 | (2) Any such direction—
-- src:779 | (a) must be given within twelve months of the company's registration by the name in question, and
@ref s 68(2)(a) A direction must be given within twelve months of the registration (src:776-779)
GIVEN `the date of the company's registration by the name in question` IS A DATE
      `the date of the direction` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(2)(a) the direction is given within twelve months of the company's registration by the name` MEANS
    IF `the date of the direction` AT MOST (`add months` `the date of the company's registration by the name in question` 12)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- twelve months of the registration: up to and including the same date a year later (fork 3)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be given within twelve months of the company's registration by the name in question"

-- src:778 | (2) Any such direction—
-- src:780 | (b) must specify the period within which the company is to change its name.
@ref s 68(2)(b) A direction must specify the period (src:778-780)
GIVEN `the direction specifies the period within which the company is to change its name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(2)(b) the direction specifies the period` MEANS
    IF `the direction specifies the period within which the company is to change its name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must specify the period within which the company is to change its name"

-- src:781 | (2A) The period must be a period of at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction.
@ref s 68(2A) The period: at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction (src:781-781)
GIVEN `the date of the direction` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(2A) the period meets the requirement of subsection (2A)` MEANS
    IF `the last day of the period` AT LEAST (`the date of the direction` PLUS 27)
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the period beginning with the date of the direction and ending on that day is at least 28 days
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The period must be a period of at least 28 days beginning with the date of the direction"

-- src:782 | (3) The Secretary of State may by a further direction extend that period.
-- src:783 | Any such direction must be given before the end of the period for the time being specified.
@ref s 68(3) Further direction extending the period (src:782-783)
GIVEN `the date of the further direction` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period for the time being specified` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(3) the Secretary of State may give a further direction extending the period` MEANS
    IF `the date of the further direction` AT MOST `the last day of the period for the time being specified`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- fork 2: a direction given on the last day is given before the end of the period
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such direction must be given before the end of the period for the time being specified"

-- src:784 | (4) A direction under section 67 or this section must be in writing.
@ref s 68(4) A direction under section 67 or 68 must be in writing (src:784-784)
GIVEN `the direction is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(4) the direction meets the requirement of being in writing` MEANS
    IF `the direction is in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A direction under section 67 or this section must be in writing"

-- src:785 | (5) If a company fails to comply with the direction, an offence is committed by—
-- src:786 | (a) the company, and
-- src:787 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 68(5) Failure to comply with the direction (the duty and its time limit) (src:785-787)
GIVEN `days allowed by the direction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 68(5) act`
`s 68(5) the company's duty to change its name as directed` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 68(5) change the company's name as the direction requires`
    WITHIN `days allowed by the direction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company failed to comply with the direction: an offence is committed under section 68(5)"

-- src:785 | (5) If a company fails to comply with the direction, an offence is committed by—
-- src:786 | (a) the company, and
-- src:787 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
-- src:788 | For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company.
@ref s 68(5) Failure to comply with the direction (who commits the offence) (src:785-788)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68(5) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company fails to comply with the direction`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with the direction, an offence is committed by"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN Company THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `Officer in default` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN Director THEN `liability of an officer`
         WHEN `Company secretary` THEN `liability of an officer`
         WHEN `Shadow director` THEN `liability of an officer` -- "For this purpose a shadow director is treated as an officer of the company."
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the text names the company and officers in default; it does not say that no one else commits the offence
    WHERE
        `liability of an officer` MEANS
            IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"

-- src:789 | (6) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 68(6) Offence (penalty) (src:789-789)
`s 68(6) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

