-- src:800 | (4) If the ground specified in subsection (1)(a) or (b) is established, it is for the respondents to show—
-- src:801 | (a) that the name was registered before the commencement of the activities on which the applicant relies to show goodwill; or
-- src:802 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:803 | (c) that the name was registered in the ordinary course of a company formation business and the company is available for sale to the applicant on the standard terms of that business; or
-- src:804 | (d) that the name was adopted in good faith; or
-- src:805 | (e) that the interests of the applicant are not adversely affected to any significant extent.
-- src:806 | If none of those is shown, the objection shall be upheld.
@ref s 69(4) The respondents' answers; otherwise the objection is upheld (src:800-806)
GIVEN `the ground specified in subsection (1)(a) or (b) is established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondents show that the name was registered before the commencement of the activities on which the applicant relies to show goodwill` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondents show that the name was registered in the ordinary course of a company formation business and the company is available for sale to the applicant on the standard terms of that business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondents show that the name was adopted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondents show that the interests of the applicant are not adversely affected to any significant extent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 69(4) the objection is upheld under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the ground specified in subsection (1)(a) or (b) is established`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the ground specified in subsection (1)(a) or (b) is established, it is for the respondents to show"
    ELSE IF       `the respondents show that the name was registered before the commencement of the activities on which the applicant relies to show goodwill`
              OR  `the respondents show that the name was registered in the ordinary course of a company formation business and the company is available for sale to the applicant on the standard terms of that business`
              OR  `the respondents show that the name was adopted in good faith`
              OR  `the respondents show that the interests of the applicant are not adversely affected to any significant extent`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If none of those is shown, the objection shall be upheld."
         ELSE JUST TRUE

